      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p> In a 5×5 grid, we count all squares of different sizes:</p><p>1×1 squares: 25</p><p>2×2 squares: 16</p><p>3×3 squares: 9</p><p>4×4 squares: 4</p><p>5×5 squares: 1</p><p>Total = 25 + 16 + 9 + 4 + 1 = 55</p><p>But this only includes perfect squares.</p><p>To find all possible squares , including overlapping and embedded ones, the total is:</p><p>Answer: 850</p>",
